# Fixture source vault

> Renamed to `README.md.fixture-source` so it is **not** itself imported as a
> vault note (that slot belongs to the fixture `README.md` below). Read this
> file; do not sync it.

This directory is the **source of truth** for the three exported fixtures under
`mcp_server/fixtures/{plain,encrypted,obfuscated}/`. Those fixtures are
`_all_docs` dumps of a real Obsidian LiveSync CouchDB; this is the `.md` vault
they were built from, so they can be regenerated deterministically.

It is the vault we hand-built (7 feature notes + 1 tombstone note) layered on
top of the stock Obsidian demo vault (`Adventurer/`, `Formatting/`, `Guides/`,
etc.), which supplies realistic volume, nested folders, and spaced paths.

## What each hand-built note exercises

| Note | Requirement it covers |
|------|----------------------|
| `README.md` | YAML frontmatter parsing; case-insensitive path resolution (`_id` `readme.md` vs `path` `README.md`) |
| `note-with-links.md` | Forward wikilink extraction, incl. aliased `[[note\|alias]]` |
| `linked-note.md` | Backlink target (reverse link graph) |
| `compressible-note.md` | Deflate compression round-trip |
| `multi-chunk-note.md` | Multi-chunk split (>50 chunks) + in-order reassembly + chunk-ID hashing |
| `note-with-emoji.md` | UTF-16 surrogate pairs, CJK, ZWJ sequences, chunk-boundary safety |
| `test123.md` | Tiny single-chunk note |
| `deleted-note.md` | **Soft-delete** — delete it after first sync so the export has a tombstone |

Subfolder + spaced-path coverage comes from the demo vault (e.g.
`Formatting/Code block.md`).

## Rebuild & re-export procedure

Do this once per config — `plain`, `encrypted`, `obfuscated` — each into its own
throwaway CouchDB database.

1. **Import** this directory as an Obsidian vault (copy the `.md` files into a
   fresh vault folder; do not copy this `README.md.fixture-source`).
2. **Configure LiveSync** for the target config and point it at an empty DB:
   - `plain` — E2EE **off**, Path Obfuscation **off**.
   - `encrypted` — E2EE **on**, Path Obfuscation **off**.
   - `obfuscated` — E2EE **on**, Path Obfuscation **on** (enables Property
     Encryption of the metadata blob).
   - Passphrase for both encrypted configs: `ThisIsMyObsidianNotebook1234`
3. **Sync** (replicate) so every note + chunk lands in CouchDB.
4. **Create the tombstone:** delete `deleted-note.md` in Obsidian, then sync
   again. LiveSync writes `deleted: true` rather than purging, so the export
   captures it.
5. **Export** from CouchDB into the matching fixture dir:
   - `all_docs.json` ← `GET /<db>/_all_docs?include_docs=true`
   - `sync_parameters.json` ← `GET /<db>/_local/obsidian_livesync_sync_parameters`
     (carries `pbkdf2salt` + `protocolVersion`; required for decryption)

`scripts/load_fixture.py` reads these back; the integration tests
(`tests/test_integration_{plain,encrypted,obfuscated}.py`) validate them.
